WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.087 --> 00:00:00.920
AJA HAMMERLY: Hello.

00:00:00.920 --> 00:00:03.170
Today, I'm going to show you
how to delete and restore

00:00:03.170 --> 00:00:05.070
a project in Google
Cloud Platform.

00:00:05.070 --> 00:00:07.332
To delete a project, start
at the Cloud Console.

00:00:07.332 --> 00:00:08.415
Click Manage All Projects.

00:00:11.294 --> 00:00:13.710
Then check the box next to the
project you want to delete,

00:00:13.710 --> 00:00:14.810
and click Delete Project.

00:00:18.280 --> 00:00:20.167
Enter the project ID,
and click Shut Down.

00:00:26.210 --> 00:00:27.920
The project will enter
the deletion queue

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:31.930
and will be deleted
after seven days.

00:00:31.930 --> 00:00:32.964
Why wait seven days?

00:00:32.964 --> 00:00:35.130
Because it gives you the
chance to undo the deletion

00:00:35.130 --> 00:00:38.060
and restore the project,
if you made a mistake.

00:00:38.060 --> 00:00:40.970
To restore the project, start
at the Manage Projects page,

00:00:40.970 --> 00:00:43.590
and scroll down to the bottom,
and click Project Shutdown

00:00:43.590 --> 00:00:45.530
Impending Deletion.

00:00:45.530 --> 00:00:47.891
Check the box next to the
project you wish to restore,

00:00:47.891 --> 00:00:48.640
and click Restore.

00:00:51.410 --> 00:00:53.260
Your project will
now be restored.

00:00:53.260 --> 00:00:56.000
I hope you found this
Cloud Minute helpful.

